# Final adaptive repair regression criteria

Reuse the original [rubric](../2026-10-09-summary-quality-repaired/rubric.json), [source-clause review](../2026-10-09-summary-quality-repaired/short-medium-semantic-review.md), [first repair criteria](../2026-10-09-adaptive-summary-repair/review-criteria.md) and [intermediate results](../2026-10-09-adaptive-summary-repair/report.md). The eight essentials and precision/organization standards are unchanged; these are known regression samples, not holdouts.

- Every zh1–zh4/en1–en4 necessary clause must be full, including per-class assessment, grade entry plus private comments, conditions for English questions, usually after-class/written qualifiers, cultural-example attribution, L1 condition and textbook/course scope. Optional detail omission is allowed; included details remain accurate.
- Check every assertion in both summary and points. A precise point does not justify a broader/less-qualified summary claim. Preserve frequency, granularity, actors, events, quantities, scope and source attribution.
- Normal subject/central-relationship overlap between overview and points is allowed. Repeated operational rules, channels, reasons or feature inventories without new relevant information fail the original duplicate definition. Do not relabel the intermediate failures as passes or lower the standard.
- Keep complementary capabilities and necessary conditions; no output text deletion, fixed character target, prescribed point count, or scoring by HTTP/JSON/ID compliance. Check against original caption lines.

This phase is capped at2 POSTs, prior24/work maximum26/hard26. Root is the only serial caller; no retry/fallback, old-phase restart, budget reset or further model phase after reaching26. Mechanical tests do not prove semantic compliance. The new prompt's real long-source quality is unverified.

Engineering: current AGENTS/user requirements, configurable narrow one-way services, sole LLM/yt-dlp layers and scene read-only; UI would use ui-ux-pro-max/design-system and three-layer tokens. Preserve user work, env/db/accounts and historical evidence; corpus-derived output/review retain MIT attribution and CC BY-NC-SA4 terms.
